  "track": "track-03",
  "title": "inserts updates deletes merges and bulk operations",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "DML changes persistent state, so explicit predicates, stable keys, transactions, and concurrency assumptions are essential. A missing filter can alter or remove every row.",
    "INSERT adds rows, UPDATE changes matching rows, and DELETE removes them; OUTPUT and row counts can help verify affected data but must be interpreted with trigger and transaction behavior in mind.",
    "MERGE combines match-based actions but can have concurrency and duplicate-source hazards. Separate DML with unique constraints may be easier to reason about.",
    "Bulk loading trades per-row flexibility for throughput and has important format, validation, locking, logging, permission, and recovery considerations.",
    "Retries after a timeout can repeat a committed operation unless the operation is idempotent or its outcome is checked."
  ],
